From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: android-kitkat-tls12 <android-kitkat-tls12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] Drop the unused AddressUtils.isLiteralIpAddress

The SNI-by-default port (libcore/0013) copied AddressUtils from Android 6.0 whole,
including isLiteralIpAddress with its 2 KB IPv4/IPv6 regex and the
cached Pattern, and AddressUtilsTest's five test_isLiteralIpAddress_*
methods. Nothing in production calls it: isValidSniHostname rejects IP
literals through Platform.isLiteralIpAddress (InetAddress.isNumeric, no
lookup), which is what 6.0 does on Android too. Removed with its tests;
AddressUtilsTest keeps the 7 isValidSniHostname tests.

Android 4.3 port (android-4.3_r3) of patch 0030 of the 4.4 series
(renumbered: the 4.4 patch 0025, the ssl.SocketFactory.provider hook of
the TLS 1.3 layer, is not part of this series). Paths and names:
libcore/crypto of 4.4 (org.conscrypt, org_conscrypt_NativeCrypto.cpp in
libjavacrypto) is libcore/luni on 4.3
(org.apache.harmony.xnet.provider.jsse,
org_apache_harmony_xnet_provider_jsse_NativeCrypto.cpp in libjavacore).
Otherwise the same change; only line offsets differ.
---
 .../xnet/provider/jsse/AddressUtils.java      | 22 ----------
 .../xnet/provider/jsse/AddressUtilsTest.java  | 42 -------------------
 2 files changed, 64 deletions(-)

diff --git a/luni/src/main/java/org/apache/harmony/xnet/provider/jsse/AddressUtils.java b/luni/src/main/java/org/apache/harmony/xnet/provider/jsse/AddressUtils.java
index 94b961cb9..96d496278 100644
--- a/luni/src/main/java/org/apache/harmony/xnet/provider/jsse/AddressUtils.java
+++ b/luni/src/main/java/org/apache/harmony/xnet/provider/jsse/AddressUtils.java
@@ -16,20 +16,10 @@
 
 package org.apache.harmony.xnet.provider.jsse;
 
-import java.util.regex.Pattern;
-
 /**
